    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Did you have similar trouble sitting still or staying focused back when you were a child?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, definitely. Even in elementary school, I was the kid who just couldn't stay in my seat to save my life. I was always wandering around the room, looking at whatever. I remember my third-grade teacher, Mrs. Gable, she had this huge glass tank with a bearded dragon in it. His name was Spike, I think? I used to just get up and go stare at him right in the middle of math. She was always sending notes home to my mom because I kept blurting things out and talking right over her. My mom used to get so mad about those notes. She’d stick them on the fridge with these little magnet clips. We had this one magnet that looked like a slice of pizza, and it actually smelled like pizza for like, years. I always wondered what kind of chemicals they use to make plastic smell like pepperoni. It's probably toxic, honestly, especially in a factory. I work around some weird smelling stuff on the production line now, actually. But yeah, what were we talking about? Oh, right, being a kid. Yeah, I was always getting notes sent home for wandering off and talking.",
