    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often find yourself making careless mistakes or having trouble organizing your daily tasks and activities?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Not really, no. I mean, my job on the line is pretty straightforward, so there isn't really much for me to organize, you know? I just stand at my station and pop these little rubber seals onto the metal caps as they come down the belt. It's super repetitive. The seals come in these huge bins, and sometimes they get all stuck together if it's too humid in the plant. The AC actually broke last month and it was just miserable in there. We had to keep the big loading dock doors wide open to get any air, and this stray cat kept wandering inside. We named him Barnaby. He was this big orange tabby, missing half an ear. I tried to give him some of my turkey sandwich on my break, but he just sniffed it and walked away. Cats are so weirdly picky, right? My aunt had a cat that would only eat if you put the food on a special ceramic plate. She lived down in Florida, though, so I guess she could afford to spoil it... wait, what did you ask me? Something about making mistakes? Yeah, no, I don't really have a problem with that.",
