    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel restless inside, like you are constantly on the go or driven by a motor?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, all the time. It's like... if I try to just stand still by the machine, or if they make us sit through those long safety training videos, it feels like this intense pressure just starts building up inside my body. Like I physically have to move, or pace, or stretch, or just go do something right that second. Speaking of those training videos, they are so outdated. The actors in them have these huge cell phones and hairstyles from like the 90s. One of the guys in the forklift safety video looks exactly like my uncle Rick. Uncle Rick actually used to drive a forklift at a lumber yard before he hurt his back. He slipped on some ice in his driveway, not even at work. It was a whole big mess with his insurance. He had to wear this huge brace for like six months and he couldn't even drive his truck. He loved that truck, too. It was this bright cherry red Chevy. I've always wanted a red car, but my insurance would probably be so high. Red cars get pulled over more, right? Or is that just a myth? I read somewhere that silver is actually the most common car color. Anyway... what was the question? Oh, right, the restless thing. Yeah, I just can't stand still, it drives me crazy.",
