    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Do you ever have periods where you need much less sleep than usual, like only two or three hours, and still feel completely energized?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I definitely need my sleep. If I don't get at least like six or seven hours, I'm a total zombie on the line. I actually just got a new mattress, too, because my old one had this huge dip right in the middle. It was one of those memory foam ones that comes rolled up in a cardboard box? It's so crazy how they vacuum seal those things. When you cut the plastic, it just goes *whoosh* and inflates all at once. My friend Sarah helped me unbox it in my apartment, and she almost got smacked in the face when it popped open. \n\nSarah's always getting into weird accidents like that, honestly. Last year she tripped over her own dog and sprained her wrist right before we were supposed to go to this concert. It was an outdoor country music thing, which I don't even really like country that much, but the tickets were free. I think a local radio station was giving them away. They do those call-in contests, you know? Like, be the ninth caller to win. I tried to win tickets to a comedy show once and dialed the number like fifty times, but all I got was a busy signal. Do people even use landlines anymore to get busy signals? My grandma still has one. It's an actual rotary dial phone, which takes forever to use if there's a lot of nines in the number. \n\nWait... what were we talking about? Oh, sleep. Right. Yeah, no, I don't ever feel energized on just two hours. I'd be completely dead.",
